course: dictionary
lesson: 10613
title: Unemployment: when work is hard to find
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unemployment means wanting a paid job, being able to work, and not having one. The clues are in the sentence around the word. «Unemployment means not having a paid job when you want one» tells you the person is looking for work.
explain: Unemployment often happens through no fault of the person. «It can happen to anyone, often through no fault of their own, when a factory closes, a shop shuts or times get hard.» So a person can be unemployed even if they worked hard and did nothing wrong.
explain: News reports often give unemployment as a rate. «The unemployment rate is the percentage of people looking for work who don't have it; 4% means 4 out of every 100.» Always ask what the number is counting.
fact: Unemployment means not having a paid job when you want one and can work.
fact: «Unemployment» can also mean the number or share of people in a country who have no job but are looking for one.
fact: «Redundancy» is losing your job because it is no longer needed. It is one reason people become unemployed.
fact: In the US and Canada, «unemployment» can mean money from the government for people who lost their job.
exercise: Unemployment means what? | Working very hard at school | Having a job you do not enjoy | Losing your home because of rent | *Wanting a paid job but being unable to find one
exercise: «When the factory closed, unemployment went up in the town.» What went up? | The number of factories in the town | *The number of people with no job who are looking for one | The price of bread | The length of the school holidays
exercise: Mia's dad lost his job, so the family is worried about money. What is the family facing? | A birthday party | A new school | A boom | *Unemployment
test: The news says the unemployment rate is 4%. What does 4% mean? | 4 out of every 10 people have a job | *4 out of every 100 people looking for work do not have it | Prices went up by 4 pence | There are 4 jobs in the whole town
test: In the US and Canada, «he's on unemployment» means what? | He is a teacher with no class | He is on holiday from school | He has found a new job and started work | *He gets money from the government because he lost his job
exam: Which situation is unemployment? | A man who retired and now enjoys his garden | *An adult who wants a paid job but cannot find one | A child who is too young to have a paid job | A woman who chooses to study full time
